# What NOT to upload when deploying from the Vercel CLI.
#
# The CLI does NOT read .gitignore — it needs this file — and without it
# `vercel --prod` tries to upload the entire working directory. That fails, and
# the error names a size limit rather than a filename:
#
#   Error: File size limit exceeded (100 MB)
#
# The offender is node_modules/@next/swc-darwin-arm64/next-swc.darwin-arm64.node,
# Next's platform-native compiler, which is over the 100 MB per-file cap on its
# own. The two build caches add several hundred MB more.
#
# None of it is wanted on the server anyway: Vercel runs `npm install` from
# package-lock.json (so it fetches the LINUX swc binary, not the macOS one) and
# `next build` fresh. Uploading a local build would at best be ignored and at
# worst be wrong for the target platform.
#
# Note that deployments triggered by a git push skip this path entirely —
# Vercel clones from GitHub and nothing is uploaded from here. This file only
# matters for CLI deploys.

# Dependencies — Vercel installs these itself
node_modules

# Build output and caches — Vercel builds fresh. Covers .next, .next-verify
# and .next-qa-dev.
.next
.next-*

# Version control — Vercel does not need the history to build
.git

# Test artefacts
coverage
test-results
playwright-report
blob-report
.playwright

# Local tooling and editor state
.vscode
.claude
.DS_Store
*.log
*.tsbuildinfo
